	(text "DESIGN NOTE:\nRotary Encoder RC Filter:\nDefault: 1k + 10nF\nMore noise filtering: 1k + 47nF\nPlace the cap close to the RP2354 ADC pin.\n\nIf Rtop = 10k\nNo contact:       ~3.30V\n20k contact:      ~2.20V\n10k contact:      ~1.65V\n10k || 20k:       ~1.32V\n\nThen firmware watches the voltage bucket sequence:\nIdle -> A -> A+B -> B -> Idle\nIdle -> B -> A+B -> A -> Idle\n\nSample PREVIOUS/NEXT at around 1 kHz,\nclassify voltage buckets, and debounce in firmware.\nThis hardware is clean enough for that."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 183.388 133.096 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "37c6ab5a-11b5-4527-b1e9-31faef4be9aa")
	)
	(text "LAYOUT NOTE:\nKeep resistors as close\nto the choke footprint\nas possible."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 251.46 217.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "77d708be-e3c1-404c-b985-8a2347dc4477")
	)
